course: dictionary
lesson: 331
title: Animation: pictures that move
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Animation is a noun with three meanings in the dictionary: a cartoon or film made from many pictures shown one after another, the art of making such films, or liveliness in the way someone talks or moves. The words around it tell you which meaning fits.
explain: «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation, like a flip book.» The clues are pictures, quickly and flip book, so animation means a moving picture made from many still pictures. Check by swapping in your meaning: "makes a film from many pictures, like a flip book" still makes sense.
explain: «Her animation made the whole class laugh.» There are no films here. Her, class and laugh show that animation means liveliness and excitement in the way she talked or moved.
fact: Animation means showing many still pictures one after another so they seem to move.
fact: «A flipbook shows how animation works: still pictures shown quickly look like movement.»
fact: Your eyes and brain blend the pictures together, so movement seems to happen.
fact: «Toy Story», made by Pixar in 1995, was the first full-length film made entirely by computer animation.
fact: Stop-motion animation uses clay figures moved a tiny bit at a time, and computer animation uses computer pictures.
exercise: «Swapping quickly between costumes, slightly different pictures of a sprite, makes animation, like a flip book.» What does animation mean here? | A kind of paper used for drawing | *A film made from many pictures shown quickly, so they seem to move | A computer that is switched off | Someone who is very lively and talks a lot
exercise: «Her animation made the whole class laugh.» What does animation mean here? | A quiet, sleepy feeling | Cartoon films about animals | *Liveliness and excitement in the way she talked or moved | The art of drawing with pencils
exercise: Which of these is an example of stop-motion animation? | A map of the town | A photo of a mountain | *A clay figure moved a tiny bit each time and photographed | A sentence written in a book
test: «Scratch was made at MIT in the USA and launched in 2007, and millions of young people use it to make games, stories and animations.» What can young people make with Scratch? | Tents and boats | *Games, stories and animations | Maps of the moon | Cakes and biscuits
test: «Toy Story», made by Pixar in 1995, was the first full-length film made entirely by computer animation. Which film was this? | Suspended animation | A flip book | *Toy Story | Scratch
exam: «A flipbook shows how animation works: still pictures shown quickly look like movement.» Which word tells us the pictures do not move on their own? | flipbook | works | *still | movement
